									<p style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7C3AED;margin:0"><span style="display:inline-block;width:22px;height:3px;background:linear-gradient(100deg,#FF2E7E,#7C3AED);border-radius:2px;margin-right:8px;vertical-align:middle"></span>Why niche wins</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7e395c81 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="7e395c81" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Why a hammam center's <span class="hl">booking logic is genuinely different</span></h2>				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-7c72e77f e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="7c72e77f" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-10cb8a37 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="10cb8a37" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-64b4da4f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="64b4da4f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>A traditional hammam center runs on gender-segregated hours, bundled day packages, and frequent group bookings — a scheduling and marketing structure that a single-chair salon booking system simply isn&#8217;t built for.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3d347168 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="3d347168" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Segregated scheduling has to be built in, not bolted on</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5ff225ea elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="5ff225ea" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Ladies&#8217; and men&#8217;s sessions typically run on separate hours or in separate facilities, and a booking flow that doesn&#8217;t clearly show which slots apply to which segment creates real friction and lost bookings.</p>								</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-61983510 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="61983510" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h3 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Groups and tourists are a genuinely different acquisition channel</h3>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f4cad87 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="f4cad87" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p>Bridal parties book weeks ahead through referral and Instagram; tourists discover through TripAdvisor and hotel concierges. Both need dedicated content and review-management attention that a purely local-SEO strategy misses.</p>								</div>
				</div>
		<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-70b046c1 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child" data-id="70b046c1" data-element_type="container" data-e-type="container" data-settings="{&quot;background_background&quot;:&quot;classic&quot;}">
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-4c3e5fcc elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="4c3e5fcc" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
									<p style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:18px;color:#fff;margin:0 0 14px">Hammam centers, at a glance</p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:130px">Segregated</b><span>— ladies &amp; men&#8217;s hours need separate booking logic</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:130px">AED 150-600</b><span>— real Dubai price range across packages</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:130px">3-6 wks</b><span>— typical ladies&#8217; session rebooking cycle</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);font-size:14px;color:#D9D5E4"><b style="font-family:Space Grotesk,sans-serif;color:#C6F432;min-width:130px">Group-heavy</b><span>— bridal &amp; family party bookings are core, not incidental</span></div>								</div>
				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
				</div>
